#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413441} :activity/id #uuid "8aa994fd-2bb6-5474-8e58-23decc01455c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049727 :topic/id #uuid "0e6d0d09-5c9c-596c-83ce-4f15c32fd909" :topic/math-academy-id 6689} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413441 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a65f23d9-ece1-5d94-9f1b-4fa3ff21de35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391389} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9d2a40-8db7-58a2-965b-5f8b9284015a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391390} {:answer/id #uuid "04c655f7-87ce-528a-8800-3f6394ecdb07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391391} {:answer/id #uuid "f96ae150-da92-5738-ba1d-d4d1763de606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391392} {:answer/id #uuid "838f71c2-360e-538a-95d7-8b3b5dc7a597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391393}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391392} :answer-field/id #uuid "df1f67de-316f-5c29-b742-1caa63eae0d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c3e7b77a-8724-5c98-839a-9b13b32a04b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-334077" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}\\sqrt{y},\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "17e3c9fb-5004-5b6c-9abb-f74c6a155256" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413442}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413442 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308555 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a87b41-81d8-5f96-86cd-025b9c0b9dba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305164} {:answer/id #uuid "3f6a5683-9ee1-5947-b947-fcf1a8f2e101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305768} {:answer/id #uuid "70e24b12-cff1-552a-8352-837e273c1845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306228} {:answer/id #uuid "779542c4-9213-5e22-a1d3-6b9f712a5f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306287} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1085e2-2118-5ddc-a2d2-87792732c5d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307490}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305164} :answer-field/id #uuid "5810ab1d-8820-5650-86eb-5e9d43366c36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0755b082-c081-5233-b79a-1dd852af7280" :question/math-academy-id "q-334080" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-y,\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example  $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({x}^{2}-y)+({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}})=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}).\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{2}-1+{2}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}) \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}(0+4-{y}_{\\text{new}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c10d508e-2b41-5faa-9b45-2844e60e0e0f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413443}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413443 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20fc8c65-780c-5c34-b5be-571c2a7b85bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305470}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305470} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f75cf12-8b61-51e6-bed9-8d88af4bba7d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5cdf480b-e736-5530-b72b-9719ec66981a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334469" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3x-{y}^{3},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(1).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(1)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((3x-{y}^{3})+(3{x}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.5x-0.5{y}^{3}+1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+1.5x-0.5{y}^{3}+1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.5{y}^{3}-y-1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}-1.5x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.5{y}^{3}-y-1.5{x}_{\\text{new}}-1.5x.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.\n$$\n\n Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.5(1)^{3}-1-1.5\\cdot 1-1.5\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.5-1-1.5 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=1$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}.\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=1.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{3}+({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-2}{1.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(0)=1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =1 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & =1.2 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈1.179\\,747 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈1.179\\,509\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈1.18,$ rounded to two decimal places."} :step/id #uuid "fd33c32d-69d3-5f03-b417-6f28a9fbbbc5"}] :activity/title "Using the Trapezoidal Method With Newton's Method" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413440}]}
